    $ apt-cache
          show libeditreadline-dev
        

        Package: libeditreadline-dev
        

        Source: libedit
        

        Version: 3.1-20210910-1
        

        Installed-Size: 28
        

        Maintainer: LLVM Packaging Team
        <pkg-llvm-team at lists.alioth.debian.org>
        

        Architecture: amd64
        

        Depends: libedit-dev
        

        Conflicts: libreadline-dev, libreadline-gplv2-dev,
        libreadline5-dev
        

        Description-en: BSD editline and history libraries (shim
        development files)
        

        GNU readline changed its license from GPL-2 to GPL-3 with
        version 6,
        

        which excludes GPL-2-only programs from using current readline
        versions.
        

        editline resembles readline functionally and with regards to its
        API.
        

        .
        

        This is a development shim library that can be used to link a
        GPL-2-only
        

        program that depends on readline with editline.

      

    which clashes with
        libreadline-dev and hence with r-base-dev and dh-r:

        

      The following
          packages will be REMOVED:
        

         dh-r libreadline-dev r-base-dev
        

        The following NEW packages will be installed:
        

         libeditreadline-dev
        

        0 upgraded, 1 newly installed, 3 to remove and 0 not upgraded.

    Anyone with any idea about
        it?

    Cheers,

        Steffen

      

    

      

  

